### 15. ANTI-PATTERNS TO AVOID

- Copying Unseen Studio's exact visuals, 3D worlds, page composition, menu layout, text, project imagery, or signature interactions.
- Turning Rights Radar into a creative-agency portfolio instead of a clear product concept and waitlist.
- Generic SaaS card grids, centered-everything layouts, purple-to-blue gradients, oversized neon glows, or meaningless glassmorphism.
- The previous neo-brutalist treatment: thick black borders everywhere, hard cartoon shadows on every surface, rotated sticker clutter, high-saturation pop-art blocks, or intentionally rough styling.
- Overly ornate 3D scenery that obscures the product explanation or harms load time.
- Requiring users to drag, hover, hear sound, or complete an animation to reach essential information.
- Scroll-jacking, forced horizontal scrolling, long mandatory intro screens, or pinned content that blocks navigation.
- Animating every element at once or running effects off-screen.
- Fake claims, fake research, unsupported legal interpretations, invented source details, or fabricated form submissions.
- Decorative controls that do nothing, inaccessible custom cursors, low-contrast text, or motion without a content purpose.
- Claiming that tests passed without running them.

